/**
 * Compliance — the Texas Official Wood Destroying Insect Report (SPCS/T-5).
 *
 * ############################################################################
 * HELD AT NOINDEX UNTIL THE OWNER CONFIRMS THE WDI DECISION.
 * B-05 says he IS licensed in the Termite and Wood Destroying Insect Control
 * category, so he CAN lawfully perform and sign a WDIR. C-09 says he would
 * rather not. CONTENT_BRIEF section 11 holds the WDI / T-5 / realtor + lender
 * cluster until that is confirmed in writing.
 *
 * This page and /services/termite-control/wdi-inspection/ are both gated on
 * BUSINESS.owner.wdiDecisionConfirmed. Flip that ONE flag in business.ts from
 * false to true and both pages ship. Strike the WDI row from the CONTENT_BRIEF
 * held table at the same time. Nothing else needs to change.
 * ############################################################################
 *
 * Verified Aug 2026 against 4 TAC ch. 7 subchapter H div. 5 and the TDA form:
 *  - FORM: "TEXAS OFFICIAL WOOD DESTROYING INSECT REPORT", SPCS/T-5
 *    (Rev. 9/1/2020). ⚠️ T-4 is SUPERSEDED and still circulates on third-party
 *    form sites. Never publish "T-4".
 *  - §7.175(a): inspections for a WDIR must be conducted by a licensed
 *    certified applicator or technician IN THE TERMITE AND WOOD DESTROYING
 *    INSECT CONTROL CATEGORY. Trainees present must be listed by name and
 *    number on the report. "Examinations of inaccessible or obstructed areas
 *    are not required."
 *  - §7.175(b) recognised inaccessible/obstructed areas: inaccessible attics;
 *    hollow-wall interiors and the space between a floor/porch deck and the
 *    ceiling or soffit below; porte cocheres, enclosed bay windows, buttresses
 *    and similar "to which there is no access without defacing or tearing out
 *    lumber, masonry, or finished work"; behind/beneath stoves, refrigerators,
 *    furniture, built-in cabinets, insulation and floor coverings; and "areas
 *    where storage conditions or locks make inspection impracticable."
 *  - §7.175(c): report must describe the structure, give address/location, and
 *    include a DIAGRAM with approximate numerical perimeter measurements
 *    ("does not have to be to scale"), construction details, CURRENT activity,
 *    PREVIOUS activity, CONDITIONS CONDUCIVE, and inaccessible areas.
 *  - §7.175(d) mandatory areas if accessible and unobstructed: plumbing
 *    (bathroom, kitchen, laundry, other e.g. hot tub); window and door frames
 *    and sills; baseboards, flooring, walls, ceilings; entrance steps and
 *    porches; exterior of slab or foundation wall; crawl spaces (support piers
 *    incl. stiff legs, floor joists, sub floors, sill plates, foundation wall);
 *    fireplace; weep holes.
 *  - §7.175(e) conditions conducive, VERBATIM LIST: "(A) a structure with wood
 *    to ground contact; (B) formboards left in place; (C) excessive moisture;
 *    (D) wood debris under or around structure; (E) footing too low or soil
 *    line too high; (F) insufficient clearance in crawl space; (G) expansion
 *    joints or cracks in slab; and (H) decks".
 *  - §7.176(a): reports in connection with a real estate transaction MUST be
 *    on the department-prescribed form; "No alterations or revisions to the
 *    department-prescribed form are permitted"; larger graphs, photos or
 *    supporting documentation may be attached as an ADDENDUM.
 *  - §7.176(b): lenders such as the VA may require another form; that form is
 *    SUPPLEMENTAL and must be kept in the inspection file.
 *  - §7.176(d): copies for (1) the person who ordered the inspection and
 *    (2) the business files. §7.176(e): retain a MINIMUM OF TWO YEARS.
 *  - §7.177: durable sticker on the wall adjacent to the water heater,
 *    electric breaker box, or beneath the kitchen sink, giving name and licence
 *    number, date of inspection, and a statement not to remove it. It is a
 *    violation for any licensee to remove or deface a posted sticker.
 *  - Form Section 4 "Forwarded To": title company, mortgagee, purchaser of
 *    service, seller agent, buyer — but "only the purchaser of the service is
 *    required to receive a copy."
 *  - Form Section 7A independence attestation: "Neither I nor the company for
 *    which I am acting have had, presently have, or contemplate having any
 *    interest in the purchase or sale of this property."
 *  - TREC does NOT regulate WDI inspections and publishes no WDI form. A
 *    licensed home inspector may not advertise WDI inspections without the
 *    separate SPCS licence. (trec.texas.gov/node/548)
 *
 * ⚠️ §7.175(a) also carries a narrow provision specific to Real Estate
 *    Transaction Inspection Reports about when a corrective treatment may be
 *    RECOMMENDED — there must be visible evidence of active infestation, or
 *    visible evidence of previous infestation with no evidence of prior
 *    treatment. That is quoted carefully below and must not be broadened.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
